<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Drill 0007 — Creating New Blocks</title>
<style>
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
:root{
  --bg:#0d1117;--surf:#161b22;--surf2:#21262d;--surf3:#2d333b;
  --green:#34d399;--blue:#60a5fa;--yellow:#fbbf24;--red:#f87171;
  --orange:#fb923c;--purple:#a78bfa;--teal:#22d3ee;--pink:#f472b6;
  --text:#c9d1d9;--dim:#6e7681;--border:#30363d;--code:#010409;
  --mono:'Cascadia Code','Fira Mono','Consolas',monospace;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
body{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;
     background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;min-height:100vh}

/* ── SHELL ─── */
#start-screen,#drill-screen,#results-screen{max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.3rem 5rem}
.hidden{display:none!important}

/* ── START SCREEN ─── */
.logo{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.75rem;color:var(--dim);letter-spacing:.08em;margin-bottom:.5rem}
h1{font-size:1.75rem;color:#fff;margin-bottom:.3rem}
.sub{font-size:.93rem;color:var(--dim);margin-bottom:2rem}

.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:1.8rem}
.chip{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.76rem;padding:.3rem .75rem;border-radius:20px;
      border:1px solid var(--border);cursor:pointer;background:var(--surf2);
      color:var(--dim);transition:all .15s;user-select:none}
.chip.on{border-color:var(--green);background:rgba(52,211,153,.1);color:var(--green)}
.chip.all-chip{border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue)}
.chip.all-chip.on{background:rgba(96,165,250,.1)}

.opt-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;margin-bottom:1.8rem;font-size:.88rem;color:var(--dim)}
.toggle{width:38px;height:20px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--surf3);border:1px solid var(--border);
        cursor:pointer;position:relative;transition:background .15s}
.toggle.on{background:var(--green)}
.toggle::after{content:'';position:absolute;width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:50%;
               background:#fff;top:2px;left:2px;transition:left .15s}
.toggle.on::after{left:20px}
.toggle-lbl{cursor:pointer}

.begin-btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.9rem;padding:.65rem 2rem;
           border-radius:6px;border:none;background:var(--green);color:#0d1117;
           cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;transition:opacity .15s}
.begin-btn:hover{opacity:.85}
.begin-btn:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:not-allowed}

.count-note{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--dim);margin-top:.8rem}

/* ── DRILL SCREEN ─── */
.drill-header{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:.9rem}
.prog-text{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;color:var(--dim)}
.prog-bar{flex:1;height:4px;background:var(--surf3);border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden}
.prog-fill{height:100%;background:var(--green);border-radius:2px;transition:width .25s}

.q-meta{display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem}
.tag{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;padding:.18rem .52rem;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--dim)}
.tag.ch-device{border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue)}
.tag.ch-block{border-color:var(--purple);color:var(--purple)}
.tag.ch-registry{border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--yellow)}
.tag.ch-gui{border-color:var(--teal);color:var(--teal)}
.tag.ch-separation{border-color:var(--orange);color:var(--orange)}
.tag.ch-traps{border-color:var(--red);color:var(--red)}
.tag.type-mc{border-color:var(--dim)}
.tag.type-wr{border-color:var(--pink);color:var(--pink)}

.q-text{font-size:1.02rem;color:#e6edf3;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:1.1rem;line-height:1.55}

pre.snippet{background:var(--code);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;
            padding:.85rem 1rem;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;
            line-height:1.8;overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:1rem;white-space:pre-wrap}
.cm{color:#2d4a5a;font-style:italic}.kw{color:#ff7b72}.fn{color:var(--green)}
.str{color:#a5d6ff}.cls{color:var(--yellow)}.num{color:var(--orange)}.pm{color:#d2a8ff}

/* MC */
.opts{list-style:none}
.opts li{background:var(--surf2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;
         padding:.55rem 1rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;cursor:pointer;font-size:.9rem;
         transition:border-color .12s,background .12s;line-height:1.5}
.opts li:hover:not(.lk){border-color:var(--green);background:rgba(52,211,153,.06)}
.opts li.ok{border-color:var(--green);background:rgba(52,211,153,.09);color:var(--green)}
.opts li.no{border-color:var(--red);background:rgba(248,113,113,.07);color:var(--red)}
.opts li.lk{cursor:default}
.mc-fb{font-size:.84rem;margin-top:.5rem;padding:.4rem .8rem;border-radius:4px;display:none}
.mc-fb.ok{background:rgba(52,211,153,.08);color:var(--green);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.2)}
.mc-fb.no{background:rgba(248,113,113,.07);color:var(--red);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.2)}

/* Written recall */
textarea{width:100%;background:var(--surf2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;
         color:var(--text);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.84rem;padding:.7rem .9rem;
         resize:vertical;min-height:90px;outline:none;transition:border-color .15s}
textarea:focus{border-color:var(--blue)}
.wr-actions{display:flex;gap:.6rem;margin-top:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.wr-btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.77rem;padding:.3rem .75rem;border-radius:4px;
        border:1px solid var(--border);background:none;color:var(--dim);cursor:pointer;
        transition:all .14s}
.wr-btn:hover{border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue)}
.wr-btn.show-btn:hover{border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--yellow)}
.concept-hits{margin-top:.7rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.8}
.hit{color:var(--green)}.miss{color:var(--red)}
.tally{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.9rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem}
.rough-note{font-size:.74rem;color:var(--dim);margin-top:.3rem;font-style:italic}
.model-ans{margin-top:.8rem;background:var(--surf2);border:1px solid var(--border);
           border-radius:6px;padding:.8rem 1rem;font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;display:none}
.model-ans strong{color:var(--yellow)}
.self-rate{display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-top:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.sr-btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.75rem;padding:.28rem .7rem;border-radius:4px;
        border:1px solid var(--border);background:none;cursor:pointer;transition:all .14s}
.sr-knew{color:var(--green);border-color:var(--green)}
.sr-knew:hover{background:rgba(52,211,153,.1)}
.sr-review{color:var(--red);border-color:var(--red)}
.sr-review:hover{background:rgba(248,113,113,.1)}

/* Nav */
.nav-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:1.5rem}
.nav-btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.82rem;padding:.4rem 1.1rem;border-radius:5px;
         border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surf2);color:var(--dim);
         cursor:pointer;transition:all .14s}
.nav-btn:hover:not(:disabled){border-color:var(--green);color:var(--green)}
.nav-btn:disabled{opacity:.3;cursor:not-allowed}
.nav-btn.finish{border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--yellow);background:rgba(251,191,36,.07)}

/* Results */
h2{font-size:1.4rem;color:#fff;margin-bottom:.6rem}
.score-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0}
.sc-box{background:var(--surf2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;
        padding:1rem;text-align:center}
.sc-big{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);line-height:1.1}
.sc-lbl{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--dim);margin-top:.3rem}
.miss-list{margin-top:1.5rem}
.miss-list h3{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--yellow);margin-bottom:.7rem}
.miss-item{background:var(--surf2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;
           padding:.5rem .9rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.84rem}
.results-btns{display:flex;gap:.8rem;margin-top:1.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.r-btn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.84rem;padding:.5rem 1.2rem;border-radius:5px;
       border:1px solid var(--border);background:none;cursor:pointer;transition:all .15s}
.r-btn.primary{border-color:var(--green);color:var(--green)}
.r-btn.primary:hover{background:rgba(52,211,153,.08)}
.r-btn.secondary{color:var(--dim)}
.r-btn.secondary:hover{border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue)}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ══ START ══ -->
<div id="start-screen">
  <div class="logo">DRILL / 0007</div>
  <h1>Creating New Blocks</h1>
  <p class="sub">Active recall drill — device layer, block layer, registration, traps</p>

  <div class="chips" id="channel-chips">
    <span class="chip all-chip on" data-ch="all">all channels</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="device">device layer</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="block">block layer</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="registry">registration</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="gui">gui path</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="separation">device/block split</span>
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="traps">traps &amp; gotchas</span>
  </div>

  <div class="opt-row">
    <div class="toggle on" id="shuffle-tog" onclick="toggleShuffle()"></div>
    <span class="toggle-lbl" onclick="toggleShuffle()">Shuffle questions</span>
  </div>

  <button class="begin-btn" id="begin-btn" onclick="begin()">Begin drill</button>
  <p class="count-note" id="count-note">20 questions selected</p>
</div>

<!-- ══ DRILL ══ -->
<div id="drill-screen" class="hidden">
  <div class="drill-header">
    <span class="prog-text" id="prog-text">Q 1 / 20</span>
    <div class="prog-bar"><div class="prog-fill" id="prog-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="q-meta" id="q-meta"></div>
  <div class="q-text" id="q-text"></div>
  <div id="q-body"></div>

  <div class="nav-row">
    <button class="nav-btn" id="prev-btn" onclick="go(-1)" disabled>← prev</button>
    <button class="nav-btn" id="next-btn" onclick="go(1)">next →</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ══ RESULTS ══ -->
<div id="results-screen" class="hidden">
  <div class="logo">DRILL / 0007 — RESULTS</div>
  <h2>Session complete</h2>
  <div class="score-grid">
    <div class="sc-box"><div class="sc-big" id="mc-score">-</div><div class="sc-lbl">MC correct</div></div>
    <div class="sc-box"><div class="sc-big" id="wr-score">-</div><div class="sc-lbl">Written: knew it</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="miss-list" id="miss-list"></div>
  <div class="results-btns">
    <button class="r-btn primary" onclick="reviewMissed()">Review missed only</button>
    <button class="r-btn secondary" onclick="restart()">Restart from scratch</button>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// QUESTION BANK
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
const BANK = [

// ── DEVICE LAYER ──────────────────────────────────────

{ch:'device',type:'mc',
 q:'What does <code>_register(path, fn)</code> store, and when is it called?',
 opts:[
   {t:'Stores <code>fn</code> in <code>self._handlers[path.upper()]</code>; called inside <code>_setup_handlers()</code>, which is invoked by <code>super().__init__()</code>.',correct:true,why:'Correct. _register uppercases the path and inserts the handler. _setup_handlers() is called by super().__init__(), so by the time __init__ returns all handlers are registered.'},
   {t:'Stores <code>fn</code> in <code>self._handlers[path]</code> (case-preserved); called by the subclass directly in its own <code>__init__</code>.',correct:false,why:'Wrong on two counts: _register() normalizes the key to uppercase, and it should be called inside _setup_handlers(), not scattered through __init__.'},
   {t:'Stores <code>fn</code> in <code>BLOCK_REGISTRY</code>; called after <code>super().__init__()</code> once the instance is fully constructed.',correct:false,why:'BLOCK_REGISTRY is a canvas.py dict of block classes, not a handler map. _register() stores into self._handlers, not any module-level registry.'},
   {t:'Stores a string path in <code>self._commands</code>; <code>fn</code> is looked up at dispatch time from the class <code>__dict__</code>.',correct:false,why:'_register() stores the callable directly under the normalized path in self._handlers — no late lookup. self._commands is not a real attribute in BaseDevice.'},
 ]},

{ch:'device',type:'wr',
 q:'Describe the handler contract for write vs query commands. What must each type return, and what happens if a write handler returns a non-empty string?',
 concepts:[
   {label:'writes return ""',terms:['""','empty string','return ""']},
   {label:'queries return str value',terms:['query','str(','return f','return "']},
   {label:'non-empty from write echoed to caller',terms:['echo','caller','response','non-empty','append']},
   {label:'ScpiError for invalid input',terms:['scpierror','scpi_error','ScpiError','raise']},
 ],
 model:'Write handlers must return "" (empty string). The return value is collected by process() — non-empty strings, regardless of command type, are appended to the response list and returned to the caller as if they were query results. Query handlers return the value as a string (e.g. f"{self.state.voltage:.4f}"). For out-of-range or invalid input, raise ScpiError(code, message) — BaseDevice._dispatch() catches it and queues it for SYSTEM:ERROR?. Never raise plain ValueError.',
},

{ch:'device',type:'wr',
 q:'Why must <code>self.state = MyState()</code> come BEFORE <code>super().__init__()</code>? Trace exactly what breaks if the order is reversed.',
 concepts:[
   {label:'super().__init__ calls _setup_handlers',terms:['_setup_handlers','setup_handler']},
   {label:'handlers reference self.state',terms:['self.state','state']},
   {label:'crash on first dispatch not __init__',terms:['first','dispatch','process','attributeerror','attribute']},
 ],
 model:'super().__init__() calls _setup_handlers(), which registers handler methods like _volt() that close over self. Those methods are NOT called at registration time — they are just stored. So __init__ itself won\'t crash. The crash happens later, on the first process("VOLT?") call: _dispatch() calls _volt(), which reads self.state — which doesn\'t exist yet — raising AttributeError. Rule: all instance variables must be set before super().__init__().',
},

{ch:'device',type:'mc',
 q:'A device needs to support both <code>VOLT</code> and <code>SOURCE:VOLTAGE</code> routed to the same handler. Which approach is correct?',
 opts:[
   {t:'Call <code>self._register("VOLT", self._volt)</code> and <code>self._register("SOURCE:VOLTAGE", self._volt)</code> — register the same callable under both paths.',correct:true,why:'Correct. _register() can map multiple paths to the same function. There is no de-duplication check; both entries just point to self._volt.'},
   {t:'Register only the canonical long-form path and rely on SCPI abbreviation expansion inside _dispatch() to match "VOLT".',correct:false,why:'BaseDevice._dispatch() does a direct dict lookup — it does not expand SCPI short-forms. Both paths must be registered explicitly.'},
   {t:'Use <code>self._register_alias("SOURCE:VOLTAGE", "VOLT")</code> only — _register_alias() handles multi-path routing natively.',correct:false,why:'_register_alias() stores an alias, but the primary ("VOLT") must also be registered. Using only _register_alias without a primary registration means the primary path isn\'t handled.'},
   {t:'Override <code>_normalize_path()</code> to map both strings to a single canonical form before _dispatch() looks them up.',correct:false,why:'BaseDevice does not have a _normalize_path() hook that subclasses are expected to override. Multi-path support is done via multiple _register() calls.'},
 ]},

{ch:'device',type:'wr',
 q:'What is <code>_do_reset()</code> for? When is it called? Write the body of <code>_do_reset()</code> for a device whose only state is <code>self.state = MyState()</code>.',
 concepts:[
   {label:'called on *RST or reset()',terms:['*rst','rst','reset()','reset']},
   {label:'restore factory defaults',terms:['default','factory','restore','initial']},
   {label:'body: self.state = MyState()',terms:['mystate()','MyState','self.state =']},
 ],
 model:'_do_reset() is called by BaseDevice.reset(), which is triggered by *RST (the IEEE 488.2 reset command) or right-click → "Reset device". It restores the device to factory defaults. For a device with a single state dataclass, the correct body is: def _do_reset(self) -> None: self.state = MyState()',
},

{ch:'device',type:'wr',
 q:`Read this snippet from <code>silmulator/devices/power_supply.py</code>:

<pre class="snippet"><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
    self.channels: Dict[int, ChannelState] = {
        i: ChannelState() <span class="kw">for</span> i <span class="kw">in</span> range(<span class="num">1</span>, self.NUM_CHANNELS+<span class="num">1</span>)
    }
    self.selected_channel: int = <span class="num">1</span>
    <span class="kw">super</span>().__init__()</pre>

Why is the dict comprehension on lines 2-4 placed before super().__init__(), and what breaks if it's moved after?`,
 concepts:[
   {label:'super calls _setup_handlers',terms:['_setup_handlers','setup_handler']},
   {label:'handlers close over self.channels',terms:['self.channels','channels']},
   {label:'attributeerror on first dispatch',terms:['attributeerror','attribute error','dispatch','process']},
 ],
 model:'The dict comprehension builds self.channels before super().__init__() is called. super().__init__() calls _setup_handlers(), which registers handler methods (e.g. _set_voltage) that access self.channels. If self.channels were created after super(), those handlers would be registered before self.channels exists. On the first SCPI dispatch, a handler like self._set_voltage() would try to read self.channels and raise AttributeError. Same rule applies to selected_channel.',
},

// ── BLOCK LAYER ──────────────────────────────────────

{ch:'block',type:'mc',
 q:'What arguments does <code>add_port(id, label, x, y)</code> accept, and what do <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> represent?',
 opts:[
   {t:'<code>id</code>: string key; <code>label</code>: displayed text; <code>x, y</code>: fractions of BLOCK_WIDTH and BLOCK_HEIGHT (0.0–1.0).',correct:true,why:'Correct. BaseBlock.add_port() calls setPos(BLOCK_WIDTH * x, BLOCK_HEIGHT * y) on the ConnectionPort, so 0.0 is the top/left edge and 1.0 is the bottom/right edge.'},
   {t:'<code>id</code>: string key; <code>label</code>: displayed text; <code>x, y</code>: pixel offsets from the block\'s top-left corner.',correct:false,why:'x and y are fractions, not pixels. BaseBlock.add_port() multiplies them by BLOCK_WIDTH and BLOCK_HEIGHT to get pixel positions.'},
   {t:'<code>id</code>: integer index; <code>label</code>: displayed text; <code>x, y</code>: scene coordinates.',correct:false,why:'port id is a string, and x/y are fractional (relative to block size), not scene coordinates. Scene coordinates are computed from the block\'s position plus the port offset.'},
   {t:'<code>id</code>: string key; <code>label</code>: displayed text; <code>x, y</code>: fractions where x=0.5 is always centered horizontally.',correct:false,why:'x=0.5 IS centered horizontally, but x is not "always" centered — you choose any fraction from 0.0 to 1.0. The description of what x/y represent is also wrong (they are fractions of block dimensions, which is correct for x=0.5 being the center).'},
 ]},

{ch:'block',type:'wr',
 q:'What are the four overrideable hooks in <code>BaseBlock</code>? Which one is required? When does each get called?',
 concepts:[
   {label:'_setup_ports required',terms:['_setup_ports','setup_ports','required']},
   {label:'_paint_content called by paint()',terms:['_paint_content','paint_content','paint()']},
   {label:'_add_device_menu_actions called by contextMenuEvent',terms:['_add_device_menu','menu_actions','context']},
   {label:'_do_reset in device not block',terms:['_do_reset','do_reset','device']},
 ],
 model:'Four hooks: (1) _setup_ports() — REQUIRED; called by BaseBlock.__init__(); use add_port() to define connection points. (2) _paint_content(painter, rect) — optional; called by BaseBlock.paint() after the title bar is drawn; draw the instrument face with QPainter. (3) _add_device_menu_actions(menu) — optional; called by contextMenuEvent; add QAction shortcuts for common commands. (4) _do_reset() — this one lives in the DEVICE subclass (BaseDevice), not the block; triggered by *RST or right-click → Reset device.',
},

{ch:'block',type:'wr',
 q:'You call <code>send_command("OUTP ON")</code> from a right-click menu action lambda. The state changes in the device, but the block face still shows the output as OFF. What call is missing and why does it fix the problem?',
 concepts:[
   {label:'self.update() missing',terms:['self.update','update()']},
   {label:'schedules repaint via Qt event loop',terms:['repaint','schedule','event loop','qt']},
   {label:'_paint_content reads device state',terms:['_paint_content','paint_content','device state']},
 ],
 model:'self.update() is missing after send_command(). update() tells Qt to schedule a repaint of this QGraphicsItem. On the next event loop tick, Qt calls BaseBlock.paint() → _paint_content(), which reads the updated device state and redraws the block face. Without update(), Qt only repaints when it independently decides to (e.g. window resize or overlap by another window), which may never happen for a stationary block.',
},

{ch:'block',type:'mc',
 q:`This is from <code>multimeter_block.py</code>:

<pre class="snippet"><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="cls">MultimeterBlock</span>(<span class="cls">BaseBlock</span>):
    BLOCK_WIDTH  = <span class="num">200</span>
    BLOCK_HEIGHT = <span class="num">160</span>
    HEADER_COLOR = <span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">80</span>, <span class="num">50</span>, <span class="num">120</span>)

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
        <span class="kw">super</span>().__init__(<span class="cls">Multimeter</span>(), <span class="str">"Multimeter"</span>)
        self._last_reading: float = <span class="num">0.0</span></pre>

What does <code>self._last_reading</code> represent and where should it NOT be stored?`,
 opts:[
   {t:'A display cache for the last value shown on the block face; it should NOT be stored in the device (Multimeter) class.',correct:true,why:'Correct. _last_reading is a UI concern — it holds what the block last rendered, not the device\'s simulated "true" reading. The device stores truth (injected values, measurement state). Mixing these would make the device untestable without Qt.'},
   {t:'The last measured voltage from the device; it should NOT be stored in the block, only in the device.',correct:false,why:'The last measured voltage is a device concern and lives in Multimeter._injected_values / _get_reading(). _last_reading in the block is specifically a display cache, not the authoritative reading.'},
   {t:'A debounce buffer preventing rapid redraws; it should NOT be exposed outside MultimeterBlock.',correct:false,why:'It is not a debounce buffer. It is a display cache holding the last value shown on the LCD face. Debouncing is not the purpose.'},
   {t:'A copy of the device\'s authoritative state, synchronized on every repaint; it should NOT be read by _paint_content.',correct:false,why:'It is not synchronized automatically. _paint_content() may update it when it calls _get_reading(), but it is a stale cache, not a live copy of device truth.'},
 ]},

{ch:'block',type:'wr',
 q:`This snippet is from <code>multimeter_block.py</code>:

